; nucleus.s2 -- arch#314 BOOT FIXTURE (a test harness, NOT the AIENOS kernel, not an implementation destination).
; Retired when L802 step 3 (boot entry + console) exists in .om with privileged words (L408 prerequisite c).
; Written in the seed assembler asm2 because omc has no privileged words yet. Build (see build.sh):
;   cat seed/rung2/table.s2 rung3/table3.s2 rung4/table4.s2 atlas/table5.s2 table-el1.s2 nucleus.s2 | asm2.bin
; What it does, on QEMU virt (aarch64, GICv3), entered at EL1 from stage1 with MMU off, x1 = bundle length:
;  - maps itself EL1-only, the model and request regions EL1 read-only, the UART and GIC as device memory;
;  - loads the omc-compiled program ELF that follows it in the bundle into EL0 (text read-only + executable,
;    data read-write + never-executable; writable-and-executable segments are refused);
;  - answers the program's four Linux service numbers itself: read 63 (fd 0 = request stream, one line per
;    call), write 64 (fd 1/2 -> UART, ESC doubled), pread64 67 (fd 3 = model region), exit 93/94;
;    any other number returns -38; a bad buffer returns -14; a bad descriptor -9;
;  - arms a per-request deadline on the virtual timer at each fd-0 read; a program that overruns it, faults,
;    or exits non-zero is ended, accounted, and relaunched on fresh zeroed memory with the next request;
;  - prints its own lines as ESC 'N' ... '\n' (demux.om splits them from program output).
; Memory: bundle PA 0x1_0000_0000 (vectors 0x0, entry 0x800, vars +0x10000, tables +0x20000, frame +0x3f000,
; program ELF +0x100000); model PA 0x1_4000_0000; params PA 0x1_8000_0000; requests PA 0x1_8010_0000;
; user text backing 0x40400000 (2 MiB max), user data backing 0x40600000 (up to 0x1_0000_0000).
; Every instruction name is a line of the tables above; each table line names its Arm DDI 0487 M.d section.
;
; ---- 0x000 vector table: 16 entries of 0x80 bytes (D1.3.1 / VBAR_EL1 needs 2 KiB alignment) ----
:VEC0
